      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:28:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If FFA_MEM_FRAG_RX is returned, you also need to check that the sender, handle and offset being requested is what you expect. If the SPMD returns something unexpected (but not a failure) and you need to abort, you should probably call FFA_MEM_RECLAIM to clear up the state in the SPMD.",
